    "chunk_size_bytes": 1689,
    "chunk_text": "National Shoora Council condemns \u2018unprovoked\u2019 Israeli-US war on Iran\n\nThe National Shoora Council (NSC) in a statement has condemned the unleashing of an unprovoked war on Iran by Israel and the US, beginning 28 February.\n\nIt said the war would result in countless deaths of innocent civilians across the Middle East, endangering also the lives of millions of marginalised Asians, including Sri Lankans, employed in the Arab world, while escalating further the oil prices that would economically hit countries world-wide.\n\nOn Saturday morning, Israel attacked a school in South Iran killing nearly 60 girls\u2013students in the primary school. The US followed by bombing the office of Iran\u2019s Supreme Leader, killing Iran\u2019s leader Imam Khamenei, aimed at a forcible regime change in the Islamic Republic, launched by these foreign colonising powers.\n\nSri Lanka, struggling to come out of economic bankruptcy, would be amongst the worst hit by this reckless US-Israeli war in the Middle East, let loose by the world\u2019s arms mafia, hours after Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi rejoiced with Israeli PM Netanyahu, having signed 16 Agreements of Cooperation with Israel, globally perceived as an apartheid State, that had destroyed Palestine and committed to systemically grabbing Arab lands in the rest of the Middle East.\n\nUS Secretary of State Marco Rubio\u2019s controversial speech delivered at the Munich Security Conference on 14 February is being seen as reigniting settler colonial control of non- white people worldwide as the dominant US-European strategy for the next hundred years. The US and Israel have already marginalised the UN to the detriment of third world countries."
  },
